(=== UNIT 1: FOUNDATIONS OF LEARNING, CREATIVITY & DESIGN THINKING ===) Tj
T*
/F1 9 Tf
() Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
/F2 9.5 Tf
(>> 1.1 Cognitive Processing Dynamics: Focused vs. Diffuse Thinking Modes) Tj
T*
/F1 9 Tf
() Tj
T*
(Design Thinking is an iterative, human-centered cognitive methodology that tackles) Tj
T*
(complex, ambiguous, ill-defined \('wicked'\) problems by deeply understanding user needs,) Tj
T*
(reframing problem spaces, and generating non-obvious innovative solutions.) Tj
T*
(* Neurological Foundations of Learning: Neuroscientist Dr. Barbara Oakley) Tj
T*
(characterizes brain processing into two complementary cognitive modes:) Tj
T*
(- Focused Mode: Highly attentive, analytical state utilizing pre-frontal cortex neural) Tj
T*
(networks. Engaged when executing structured, familiar algorithms, debugging syntax, or) Tj
T*
(performing direct mathematical calculations along established neural pathways.) Tj
T*
(- Diffuse Mode: Relaxed, resting-state neural network \(Default Mode Network - DMN\).) Tj
T*
(Occurs during mind wandering, walking, or sleep, facilitating broad subconscious) Tj
T*
(connections between disparate cognitive domains. Crucial for out-of-the-box creative) Tj
T*
(breakthrough.) Tj
T*
(* Learning Frameworks: The VARK Model categorizes perceptual modalities into Visual) Tj
T*
(\(diagrams, flowcharts\), Auditory \(discussions, podcasts\), Read/Write \(documentation,) Tj
T*
(notes\), and Kinesthetic \(physical building, prototyping\). Effective design teams) Tj
T*
(synthesize multi-modal communication.) Tj
T*
(* Cognitive Biases and Blocks: \(1\) Functional Fixedness: Mental bias restricting) Tj
T*
(individuals to perceive an object solely in its traditional intended role \(e.g.,) Tj
T*
(viewing a smartphone only as a telephone rather than an environmental sensor array\).) Tj
T*
(\(2\) Einstellung Effect: Predisposition to apply a previously mastered habitual) Tj
T*
(solution to a new problem even when simpler or superior alternatives exist.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
/F2 9.5 Tf
(>> 1.2 Creativity, Invention and Innovation Taxonomy) Tj
T*
/F1 9 Tf
() Tj
T*
(* Creativity: The mental capacity to conceive novel, surprising, and valuable ideas) Tj
T*
(or conceptual connections.) Tj
T*
(* Invention: The physical creation of a totally novel mechanism, composition, or) Tj
T*
(device that never existed before \(patentable artifact\).) Tj
T*
(* Innovation: The commercialization and socio-technical adoption of creative ideas) Tj
T*
(that deliver scalable human value and solve real-world problems: Innovation =) Tj
T*
(Invention x Commercialization x Adoption.) Tj
T*
(* Types of Innovation: \(1\) Incremental Innovation: Small, continuous improvements to) Tj
T*
(existing products \(e.g. optimizing database query speed\). \(2\) Disruptive / Radical) Tj
T*
(Innovation: Paradigm-shifting breakthroughs creating entirely new market categories) Tj
T*
(\(e.g. cloud computing replacing on-premise servers\).) Tj
T*
ET

