(>> 1.3 Methodological Frameworks: Stanford d.school and IDEO) Tj
T*
/F1 9 Tf
() Tj
T*
(* Stanford d.school 5-Stage Framework: \(1\) Empathize \(understand users\), \(2\) Define) Tj
T*
(\(frame problem statement\), \(3\) Ideate \(diverge and generate ideas\), \(4\) Prototype) Tj
T*
(\(build low-fidelity models\), \(5\) Test \(gather feedback from real users\). The process) Tj
T*
(is non-linear and iterative.) Tj
T*
(* IDEO Human-Centered Design \(HCD\) Three Lenses of Innovation:) Tj
T*
(- Desirability: What makes human sense? Does it solve real user pain points?) Tj
T*
(- Feasibility: What is technically and functionally possible within engineering) Tj
T*
(constraints?) Tj
T*
(- Viability: What makes commercial and economic sense for long-term sustainability?) Tj
T*
(- The Innovation Sweet Spot lies at the exact intersection of Desirability, Feasibility,) Tj
T*
(and Viability.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
/F2 9.5 Tf
(>> 1.4 Global Case Studies in Successful vs. Failed Design) Tj
T*
/F1 9 Tf
() Tj
T*
(* Case Study 1 \(Success\): Apple iPod and iTunes Ecosystem \(2001\). Replaced clunky MP3) Tj
T*
(players with seamless human-centered hardware scroll-wheel ergonomics paired with an) Tj
T*
(ecosystem software store for purchasing single songs legally.) Tj
T*
(* Case Study 2 \(Failure\): Google Glass \(2013\). High technical feasibility but total) Tj
T*
(failure in human empathy and social desirability: awkward intrusive aesthetics,) Tj
T*
(privacy infringement concerns, and lack of clear daily use-cases resulted in market) Tj
T*
(rejection.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
/F2 9.5 Tf
(-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
/F1 9 Tf
/F2 9.5 Tf
([CASE STUDY 1: GE Healthcare Adventure Discovery Series MRI]) Tj
T*
/F1 9 Tf
/F2 9.5 Tf
(-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
/F1 9 Tf
(Problem Context: Doug Dietz, chief designer of MRI scanners at GE Healthcare, discovered) Tj
T*
(that over 80% of pediatric patients required heavy chemical sedation due to paralyzing) Tj
T*
(terror when placed inside cold, noisy, intimidating cylindrical MRI machines. The) Tj
T*
(medical and financial costs of pediatric anesthesia were enormous.) Tj
T*
(Design Thinking Intervention:) Tj
T*
(Empathize Phase: Dietz spent weeks observing hospitalized children in oncology wards,) Tj
T*
(interviewing child psychologists, pediatric nurses, and parents.) Tj
T*
(Define Phase: Problem Reframed: 'How might we transform the frightening MRI clinical) Tj
T*
(procedure into an engaging, magical adventure for young children?') Tj
T*
(Ideate Phase: Brainstormed narrative-driven visual themes with museum docents,) Tj
T*
(children's book illustrators, and play therapists.) Tj
T*
ET

endstream
