([CASE STUDY 2: Overcoming Functional Fixedness in Smart Infrastructure]) Tj
T*
/F1 9 Tf
/F2 9.5 Tf
(-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
/F1 9 Tf
(Problem Context: A municipal civil sensor project required continuous acoustic) Tj
T*
(monitoring of bridge stay-cable tension and micro-cracking across a 3 km suspension) Tj
T*
(bridge in adverse coastal weather. Commercial accelerometers cost $2,000 per node,) Tj
T*
(exceeding municipal budget.) Tj
T*
(Design Thinking Intervention:) Tj
T*
(Identifying Cognitive Block: The engineering team suffered from Functional Fixedness,) Tj
T*
(assuming vibration sensing required specialized military-grade piezoelectric) Tj
T*
(transducers.) Tj
T*
(Diffuse Thinking & Cross-Domain Analogy: The team examined consumer smartphones,) Tj
T*
(recognizing that mass-manufactured automotive MEMS accelerometers in smartphones cost) Tj
T*
(under $3.00 while delivering 16-bit tri-axial measurement.) Tj
T*
(Solution Architecture: Embedded ruggedized ESP32 microcontrollers paired with consumer) Tj
T*
(MEMS sensors housed in waterproof 3D-printed enclosures running solar-powered wireless) Tj
T*
(mesh networking.) Tj
T*
(Measurable Results: Sensor unit cost decreased from $2,000 to $45.00 \(a 97.7% cost) Tj
T*
(reduction\), enabling 200 distributed sensing nodes across the bridge instead of just 4.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
/F2 9.5 Tf
(-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
/F1 9 Tf
/F2 9.5 Tf
([CASE STUDY 3: The Design Failure of the Segway Personal Transporter]) Tj
T*
/F1 9 Tf
/F2 9.5 Tf
(-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
/F1 9 Tf
(Problem Context: In 2001, the Segway personal mobility device was hyped as a) Tj
T*
(revolutionary invention that would fundamentally replace urban automobiles. Despite) Tj
T*
($100M invested, it failed commercially.) Tj
T*
(Root-Cause Failure Analysis across IDEO 3 Lenses of Innovation:) Tj
T*
(Feasibility Lens: Outstanding engineering; gyroscopic self-balancing was a triumph of) Tj
T*
(control engineering.) Tj
T*
(Viability Lens: Terrible unit economics; launched at $5,000 retail, far beyond consumer) Tj
T*
(impulse purchases.) Tj
T*
(Desirability Lens: Catastrophic lack of user empathy; it had no natural infrastructure) Tj
T*
ET

